{"id": "1f959686-a8a5-4ccf-957d-85b6e07eee63", "text": "molecular MTI markers was abolished in the fls2 mutant, which lacks the PRR receptor for flg22 peptide, and largely impaired in pfd6-1 (fig. S13). These results link PFD6 to MTI downstream of FLS2 PRR receptor function (10, 33). Collect ively, these results (Fig. 4) validate the biological significance of PPIN-1 and confirm that patho gen effectors target host proteins that are required for effective defense or pathogen fitness. To facil itate further hypothesis testing, we present the lo cal networks for the five significantly targeted hubs (Fig. 2D and table S4) and point out con nections to cellular functions potentially relevant to immune system function (figs. S14 to S18). Conclusions. Our analyses reveal that oomycete and bacterial effectors separated by ~2 billion years of evolution target an overlapping subset of 10. Glossary, materials and methods, supporting figures, and supporting tables are available as supporting material on Science Online. 11. Arabidopsis Interactome", "metadata": {"source": "data\\science.1203877.docx", "chunk_index": 0, "total_chunks": 54}, "embedding": [-0.09772782772779465, -0.0809948742389679, -0.026226408779621124, 0.0027675500605255365, 0.13464707136154175, 0.052647896111011505, -0.07144206017255783, 0.05843580514192581, 0.0966508612036705, -0.012479920871555805, 0.05339537188410759, 0.004070809576660395, 0.029350226745009422, 0.030020559206604958, 0.03800296410918236, 0.053976334631443024, -0.059601180255413055, 0.05395882949233055, 0.015576710924506187, 0.0247082207351923, 0.0111036142334342, 0.07598993182182312, -0.0043237460777163506, -0.02092752419412136, -0.0773821771144867, -0.06795459240674973, 0.012874647043645382, 0.06269001215696335, -0.04642095789313316, -0.04461856558918953, 0.027580970898270607, 0.07694579660892487, -0.009407030418515205, -0.023405946791172028, -0.0686149001121521, 0.03724060207605362, 0.09485768526792526, -0.08982834219932556, 0.0306684561073