{"id": "ed45208e-a3f8-411a-aa7c-fe67bd752648", "text": "SCIENCE VOL 333 29 JULY 2011 601 RESEARCH ARTICLES A high-quality binary protein-protein in teractome map for Arabidopsis. To generate a map of the Arabidopsis interactome network, we used a collection of ~8000 open reading frames representing ~30% of its predicted protein-coding genes (fig. S2 and table S3) (2, 3). We tested all pairwise combinations of proteins encoded by these constructs (space 1) with an improved high throughput binary interactome mapping pipeline based on the yeast two-hybrid (Y2H) system (fig. S2) (3, 4). Confirmed pairs were assembled into a data set of 5664 binary interactions between 2661 proteins, called Arabidopsis Interactome version 1 “main screen” (AI-1MAIN) (table S4). The quality of AI-1MAIN was evaluated against a positive reference set (PRS) of 118 well-documented, manually recurated (5) Ara bidopsis protein-protein interactions and a ran dom reference set (RRS) of 146 random protein pairs (fig. S3 and table S5) (3, 5–9). We deter mined the fraction", "metadata": {"source": "data\\science.1203877.docx", "chunk_index": 10, "total_chunks": 54}, "embedding": [0.010022839531302452, -0.10319215804338455, -0.01405734196305275, -0.03315345570445061, 0.0782042145729065, -0.005324108526110649, -0.05480952188372612, 0.01916499435901642, 0.00931728258728981, -0.010007044300436974, 0.03767271712422371, -0.013649141415953636, -0.011932490393519402, -0.031567707657814026, -0.011921493336558342, 0.06393443793058395, 0.0034563723020255566, 0.02093121036887169, -0.013147486373782158, -0.04508795216679573, 0.015000208280980587, 0.04968477040529251, 0.016523655503988266, -0.07623450458049774, 0.0040601263754069805, -0.01849454641342163, -0.07605558633804321, 0.00030834064818918705, -0.021652059629559517, -0.1164759024977684, 0.0012876256369054317, 0.06074462831020355, 0.054193247109651566, 0.040107980370521545, -0.041119445115327835, 0.09186728298664093, 0.04837474972009659, -0.11887942254543304