{"id": "81ab4fbc-6cf7-4af3-9e12-9f3fe89a3561", "text": "(P = 0.005, Fisher’s exact test). The interactions between the 14-3-3 proteins and the abscisic acid–responsive element binding transcription factor AREB3 are corroborated by Protein-protein interaction assigned to community: Enriched in GO annotations Not enriched in GO annotations Typical randomized network previous findings in barley (21) and suggest that plant 14-3-3 proteins mediate multiple hormone signaling pathways. Several communities, such as transcription/ gene expression and nucleosome assembly, share proteins indicating linked biological processes (fig. S36). Particularly striking is the large trans membrane transport community sharing 13 pro teins with the vesicle trafficking community Protein-protein interaction not assigned to community Protein Downloaded from https://www.science.org at University of Notre Dame on October 15, 2025 0 5 10 15 20 250 0.5 1 15 AI-1, including six novel ones (fig. S8). Where as two non-AUX/IAA interactors of TPL have been reported so far", "metadata": {"source": "data\\science.1203877.docx", "chunk_index": 22, "total_chunks": 54}, "embedding": [-0.033809494227170944, -0.10783766955137253, -0.09770790487527847, -0.019183224067091942, 0.07455367594957352, 0.07276156544685364, 0.01001331303268671, 0.01931837759912014, 0.06658494472503662, -0.02010381408035755, 0.12647055089473724, -0.03166786581277847, -0.070902980864048, 0.0468205101788044, 2.93517059617443e-05, 0.0042145210318267345, -0.07936898618936539, -0.01473203208297491, -0.03107900358736515, -0.105296291410923, -0.03751831129193306, 0.04532243311405182, 0.056229785084724426, 0.012937122024595737, 0.014622189104557037, -0.05859822407364845, -0.0842386782169342, -0.03935868293046951, 0.018207469955086708, -0.04073193669319153, -0.10781311988830566, 0.03517172113060951, -0.012211399152874947, -0.013850802555680275, -0.02180967852473259, 0.026989467442035675, -0.05923011153936386, -0.07851520925760269, 0.0388900265